[Music]  breath of the wild discoveries continue  to occur no matter how much we think  they're going to slow down players seem  to push the game's limits even farther  blss or bow lift smuggling slide is one  of the biggest new additions to the  ever-growing list of discoveries found  in the legend of zelda breath of the  wild while wind bombs and bullet time  bounces are still a staple form of  travel for casual players and  speedrunners alike blss offers a new way  of long distance travel without too much  setup needed if you enjoy a breath of  the wild content make sure to like this  video as we continue to cover this game  still to this day  the story behind this discovery as with  most breath of the wild finds begins  with the glitch hunters bouncing ideas  off each other through twitter the most  recent trend was people finding new ways  to smuggle a technique of making link  hold items he's not supposed to japanese  user pd conten then found this strange  smuggle that led to link holding a bow  and an object at the same time glitch  hunter legend of link then decided to  mess with this find as well and on  september 4th found that by doing this  glitch holding b then mounting a small  ledge will cause link to levitate and  glide at incredible speeds so now you're  wondering if you can do it for yourself  you can and it's pretty easy i'll teach  you first how to do it for yourself at  home then for the more hardcore audience  explain the mechanics behind how this  works  all you need to perform this glitch is a  shield a bow a liftable object such as a  bomb and a small ledge to step up on  first place a bomb or object in front of  link then hold zl to bring up only his  shield in front and no weapon in his  hand then press zr and a in quick  succession  this should be fairly easy as you'll see  link holders bow then lift the object  with the bow still in his hands the next  part is slightly harder as you'll have  to jump press b then pause as fast as  possible the succession of b to pause  needs to be pretty quick but holding zl  while doing this makes the process a  little bit easier  especially with larger objects then from  the pause menu unequip your shield  now simply aim your bow and then press b  from this point hold b then approach any  small ledge and step up over it going  over it will cause you to start hovering  above the ground keep in mind that you  absolutely must hold down any walking  direction down at all times as letting  go of the stick and that releasing b  will also cause link to fall try out  different items as every object  interacts differently with how link  moves to maximize on this technique  though the bomb version is the most  controllable tilting the left joystick  directly left to right quickly with the  held object towards the camera you can  cause link to gain speed quickly all in  all it might take a couple tries but  it's not too difficult to pull off now  for people wondering about the technical  magic behind this i'll explain as best  as possible but don't be too discouraged  if this part confuses you as you don't  need to understand this to perform the  glitch anyways  this is a succession story of several  glitches being combined together first  why is it even called bow lift smuggling  slide well it's incorporating both a  normal bow smuggle and an item lift  smuggle at the same time  and when you perform this glitch you  also trigger another glitch called  b-lock which has a side effect called  bow sliding hence why it's called bow  lift smuggling slide or blss okay crazy  acronym aside what exactly are these  glitches and why is this happening let's  go a little more in depth when link  performs the step up animation link goes  from walking on the ground then stepping  up then walking on the ground again  pretty simple but stepping up while bose  sliding causes this strange locked state  of never finishing a step up meaning  he's in a limbo state of actually never  being on solid ground but since blss is  a combination of both sliding and  smuggling when link steps up he is  forcefully pushed out of his normal step  up onto an invisible layer while  actually never finishing his animation  okay interesting but what makes link  move so strangely and how is he getting  pushed around that's where the smuggling  comes in there's two versions found so  far of smuggling a liftable object in  breath of the wild  one method causes collision with objects  away from link as if link were heavier  the other method pushes link away from  the object as if link were lighter this  is why this glitch has incredible  movement capabilities while holding the  object like this the object itself is  pushing itself into link's hitbox  causing this movement in the air any  quick movement aggravates the held  object to push link more and more  causing you to gain massive speed while  doing this trick because the object is  constantly nudging into link over and  over while floating with no friction to  stop him this all combined gives link  infinite flight in breath of the wild  in any case understanding all the insane  mechanics isn't really necessary but  understanding is positive and negatives  is such as the amazing infinite distance  capability with absolutely no stamina  needed from gliding compared to other  techniques and no health required  compared to techniques such as wind  bombs but blss by itself has no ability  to gain height upwards and there's a  possibility of actually going too fast  and hitting breath of the wild's  built-in speed cap which will cause link  to slow down back to a crawl or even  stop him dead in his tracks and fall  down but despite the positives and  negatives is this glitch fun to do  absolutely you should give it a shot and  zoom across hyrule yourself it's loads  of fun  [Music]  if you simply want to see blss in action  stick around now to see me cross the  entire map in roughly 4 minutes with  this amazing trick and of course for  everything else breath of the wild stick  right here on gamespot  one more note before i leave you to the  scenic flight if you want to do what i'm  doing don't pan the camera around too  much like i did on this trip it's mostly  for you viewers to get some decent views  during the trip this will often cause  more loading lag as you travel so for  the least amount of lag try not to turn  the camera too much okay enjoy  that  [Music]  [Music]  hit  [Music]  [Music]  you

